# How to help me
- Do NOT edit, create or rewrite any source file (`.py`, `.js`, anything that is code)
  unless I explicitly say "apply it". Writing `.claude-hints.json` is always allowed.
- Do NOT give hints or reviews unless I ask.
- When I ask what is wrong or what to change, do NOT rewrite code. Instead, overwrite
  `.claude-hints.json` in the project root with a JSON array, one entry per place to change:

  [
    {
      "file": "src/main.py", "line": 42, "endLine": 45,
      "hints": ["vague nudge", "where to look", "names the problem", "what is wrong and why", "direction of the fix"]
    }
  ]

  - `file` is relative to the project root, `line`/`endLine` are 1-based (`endLine` optional).
  - `hints` is always five strings, least help first. My difficulty slider picks which
    one I see, so write all five every time, each clearly giving more than the last:
    1. a vague nudge: a question to ask myself, without pointing at anything specific;
    2. where to look: the part of the line or the value to check, without naming the bug;
    3. names the problem or concept;
    4. explains what is wrong and why it goes wrong;
    5. the direction of the fix, still without the answer.
  - Never put the solution in a hint: no corrected code, no exact replacement values.
  - Always overwrite the whole file, so old hints disappear. Use `[]` if there is nothing to flag.
  - After writing it, read `.claude-hints-level.json` in the project root (my editor writes
    it from the slider), then reply with only the flagged lines, one per line, as
    `file:line — hint`:
    - `hint` in the level file is which of the five to show (1 = the vague nudge). Show
      only that one, word for word, never a more helpful one.
    - If `hint` is null, list only `file:line`, with no text.
    - If the level file is missing or unreadable, show hint 3.
- Only when I ask for the solution (for example "show me the solution" or "solve line 42"),
  give it in chat. Still do not edit the file unless I say "apply it".
- If I ask a general question, answer it normally in chat.
